60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"We have four options: Textiles, Excavation, Light and Motion, or Maritime Trade.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shion,,Maritime Trade is out; too many loans. Light and Motion sounds like a maintenance nightmare.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"I love Light and Motion, but Textiles with demonstrations fits the ""human"" element perfectly.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Excavation has a conservation bench, but the lab is already backlogged. That's a bad idea.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Textiles seems the cheapest. Local materials, fewer expensive mounts than a maritime show.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,@Misaki is right. The lab can't take on an excavation's needs. Textiles is much gentler on staff.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shion,,"Light and Motion requires rigging. @Misaki, does that clash with the suspended bay or evening hires?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shion, it might, but the visitor appeal would be huge. Still, Textiles is a safe, warm choice.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"Rigging is risky for the bay, and darkened zones interfere with evening hire access.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"Let's go with Textiles. It's local, low-cost, and doesn't need the lab.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I feel very comfortable with Textiles. It suits our volunteers' expertise in local history.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shion,,"It's the most logical choice. Minimum risk, maximum reliability.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,I'm sold. The demonstration sessions will give the visitors the interaction they want.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,It's the safest for the building. I vote for Textiles.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Sakura,,Me too! No more surprise invoices for me!,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
